ta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 6,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361636 13194139535693 true] [17592186361635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361637 13194139535693 true] [17592186361635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361638 13194139535693 true] [17592186361635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361639 13194139535693 true] [17592186361635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361640 13194139535693 true] [17592186361635 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535693 true] [17592186361635 1041 "selection" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361635 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361640 13194139535693 true] [17592186361635 1110 #uuid "86ea7f3d-e895-5646-b10c-adb24a46e87c" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361636 1034 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 9,\\,\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi /2}" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361636 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535693 true] [17592186361636 1111 #uuid "f845b37e-a469-5a63-b8cd-66cdfc73e74d" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361637 1034 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 4,\\,\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le \\pi /2,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361637 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535693 true] [17592186361637 1111 #uuid "92fbce80-ebd0-5021-a715-0dc15267520b" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361638 1034 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 6,\\,\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le \\pi /2,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi /2}" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535693 true] [17592186361638 1111 #uuid "70d86b5b-8e08-587b-8455-cc5d5b615338" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361639 1034 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 3,\\,\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le 2\\pi }" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535693 true] [17592186361639 1111 #uuid "c4ff2aca-6caa-5e35-8db5-5cd7e33fd721" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361640 1034 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 6,\\,\\pi /2\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535693 true] [17592186361640 1111 #uuid "2e5fcc02-e966-52d7-86b0-24cc45be5775" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361641 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361642 13194139535693 true] [17592186361641 1089 "q-161883" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361641 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535693 true] [17592186361641 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069421/assets/a32e8fd24c990a831cfee9525c6b1c035fb4ee6e09deedb3ac4c899d90ceeaac.png)\n\nThe solid enclosed by the half-sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+4y=0$ for $z\\le 0,$ shown above, can be described in spherical polar coordinates as" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361641 1113 #uuid "932b92db-8d77-5894-b632-3b8edb79745e" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361641 1145 "We write the position of a point (vector) in spherical polar coordinates as $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ),$ where \n\n- $\\rho \\ge 0$ is the distance from the point to the origin,\n\n- $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ is the angle between the point and the positive $x$-axis, and\n\n- $ϕ\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is the angle the corresponding vector makes with the positive $z$-axis.\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents one-half of the sphere of radius $2$ centered at $(0,-2,0).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+4y=0$ in spherical polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+4y & =0 \\\\ {\\rho }^{2}+4\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ & =0 \\\\ \\rho (\\rho +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $\\rho $ cannot be identical to zero on the entire sphere, we must have $\\rho =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069421/assets/e2865e838521a8864ad76d72e520d4b128a8fceb8c18cb9c35ba10134419c4eb.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that inside our region, the spherical polar coordinates vary within the following domains:\n\n- $\\rho \\in [0,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ]$\n\n- $\\theta \\in [\\pi ,2\\pi ]$\n\n- $ϕ\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361643 13194139535693 true] [17592186361642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361644 13194139535693 true] [17592186361642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361645 13194139535693 true] [17592186361642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361646 13194139535693 true] [17592186361642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361647 13194139535693 true] [17592186361642 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535693 true] [17592186361642 1041 "selection" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361642 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361644 13194139535693 true] [17592186361642 1110 #uuid "860a109d-2fba-5b4c-997e-048d856105e4" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361643 1034 "$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }\n$$" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361643 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535693 true] [17592186361643 1111 #uuid "96de6de2-0978-5064-a1f9-d9c36d4487e9" 13194139535693 true] [17592186361644 1034 "$$\n{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }